; seamprobe -- a FIXTURE, not a lang.
;
; tools/check/seam.sh declares %lang-root class `bundle`: bound while a bundle
; is loaded, absent in a bare dialect.  Checking the second half needs only a
; dialect boot; checking the FIRST half needs a bundle to exist, and a gate
; that must clone another repository to run is a gate that does not run.
;
; So this is the smallest thing x.sh will accept as one: a declaration and an
; entry that defines nothing.  It is deliberately NOT a surface language --
; it sets no %lang-name, claims no prompt, and must never grow one, or the
; gate starts proving things about a lang nobody uses instead of about the
; wrapper's bundle path.
;
; helium: the cheapest dialect that boots, and the probe reaches for nothing
; a tower provides.

(lang "seamprobe")
(dialect he)
(entry "run.x")
